## NEXUSAI'S RULES (verbatim from `1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md`, 2368 lines when drafted, last entry C-218 at `:2362`; RE-READ them at source in the same action as the land command and again in the same action as the Part 3 merge command, C-218; quote the line numbers you read)
- **C-190** (`:2062`): *"KAM'S RULING: GitHub's CodeQL ruleset is ORGANISATIONAL POLICY and we adhere to it. Every merge to NexusAI main goes through a PULL REQUEST, and a PR must add NO NEW high-or-higher CodeQL alert in the code it changes. Test code is included."* Item 2 (`:2067`): *"Merge path: open a PR from the gated branch, wait for CodeQL (a background wait that EXITS), then land the SAME commit. Never squash, never rebase ([[C-68]])."* Item 3 (`:2068`): *"NEVER dismiss a code-scanning alert, from any side, and never touch the ruleset."* Addendum (`:2076`): `alerts_threshold = errors`, so ANY new alert whose RULE severity is `error` blocks. A wait on the checks must require every `Analyze (<language>)` run completed (`:2073`).
- **C-68** (`:665`): *"A gate verdict is valid only at the head it ran on. … the merge condition is not "verify passes" — it is RE-RUNNING THE AFFECTED CELLS on the new head, each named individually …"* (`:666`) *"I expect them unaffected" is the sentence this rule exists to catch.* Amendment (`:668-671`): counts are regenerated ONCE, on the tree that exists AFTER the merge.
- **C-184** (`:1966-1970`): a merge author merges main FORWARD and queues its merge hold ONLY when no other seat's merge ticket is queued or holding the jest lock; read `queue-jest/` and the lock owner for tags containing `merge`, and `ls-remote` main, immediately before. A proof or gate hold ahead is fine; only another MERGE ticket blocks. Rule 4: a hold on a base that can no longer fast-forward is stopped by pid through your own ancestry, the branch returned to its gated head, never pushed.
- **C-57** (`:418-428`) and **C-112/C-133** (`:1149-1160`, `:1434-1447`): a conflict confined to `scripts/verify-expected-counts.json` is resolved by REGENERATION, never by hand-edit; the id-superset may be established by CONSTRUCTION (every `__tests__` blob equals a parent's blob) only when no test file is content-merged; otherwise the runner `c57-id-superset.sh` and `c133-accounting.py`.
- **C-209** (`:2270`, landing condition `:2273`, amendment `:2277-2281`): *"after the FF push, wait for main's push CodeQL analysis to complete, then read each claimed alert BY NUMBER. Each must read fixed on refs/heads/main. … Any still open: STOP and mail with the run id."* A PR's CodeQL run CANNOT show a PRE-EXISTING main alert as fixed; read the CodeQL check run's conclusion and the PR-ref open list before every land. (B343 landed #98 with 62 of 63 closed and #116 still open: that is the precedent for what a failed by-number read looks like; here the STOP list is the three alerts below.)
- **C-185** (`:1975-2007`): a local verify red ONLY on a known-set cell may be re-run ONCE as a fresh hold; any other failure is a STOP. **C-192** (`:2095`): "Permission denied (publickey)" is a TRANSPORT failure, retry up to 5 times about 10 s apart; GH013, "protected branch", "Repository rule violations", "rejected", non-fast-forward are STOPs; after a successful push read main back with `ls-remote`; poll main at most every 5 minutes.
- **C-218** (`:2362`): *"… read C-190 (and C-68, [[C-184]]) in the same action as the merge command; the verb is copied from the project's rule, never from the last project landed."*
Grep for a later clause: `/usr/bin/grep -n -i -E 'PR #97|rd-?774|rd-?836|C-211|counts|land' …/CLARIFICATIONS.md` and report any entry after `:2362` (positive control: the same grep over the whole file prints hits). **A rule you find that disagrees with this brief wins; STATUS says so.**

